  "card": "This PR corrects HTTP status and response formatting for malformed JSON-RPC 2.0 requests, returning HTTP 200 OK with an error payload and setting the ID to null when missing. In debug builds with authenticated RPC, sending a malformed JSON-RPC 2.0 request trips an Assume assertion and crashes bitcoind. In release builds, this fixes compliance with the JSON-RPC 2.0 specification by avoiding HTTP error status codes for malformed requests whose version is known.",
